       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5,000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day, nearly four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day (and often 3 g/day is used). For a 70 kg adult with normal liver function, that dose carries a serious risk of acute liver failure. A single 5,000 mg dose is also above the 1,000 mg standard maximum per dose, and it would be in the range where toxicity is a concern.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** by mouth, three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** by mouth, three times daily (about 2 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg** by mouth, three times daily (3 g/day), which is a common full-dose regimen\n- **1,000 mg** by mouth, four times daily (4 g/day), the maximum\n\nIf you do want the 5,000 mg dose for a reason I don't know about, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll flag it on the order. I'd still suggest pharmacy review first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
